NAME
       c2c-serve - the OpenAI-compatible front of the cache-to-cache relay

SYNOPSIS
       c2c-serve [--host HOST] [--port PORT] [--certfile FILE]
                 [--keyfile FILE] [--api-key KEY | C2C_API_KEY]
                 [--pair RECEIVER[+SHARER]] [--engine ENGINE]
                 [--config FILE] [--privacy] [--log-level LEVEL]
                 [--fuser-weights PATH]

DESCRIPTION
       The front answers on a port, and fuses the cache of the sharer
       into the state of the receiver before a single token is born.
       It speaks the OpenAI wire protocol, the routes:

       /v1/models            the models on the shelf, and the pairs
       /v1/chat/completions  the chat, the fused completion, streamed
       /v1/completions       the plain, the old completion
       /healthz              the pulse, for the probes of orchestrators

       The pair is named RECEIVER, or RECEIVER+SHARER, a name from the
       registry of the --config file. The engine names the adapter:
       hf, vllm, sglang, trtllm, llamacpp, mlx, tgx, ollama, reference.

OPTIONS
       --host HOST        the address to answer on; default 127.0.0.1,
                          and wisely so, for it is a localhost
       --port PORT        the port; default 8121
       --certfile FILE    the certificate; with --keyfile, HTTPS
       --keyfile FILE     the key; keep it secret, keep it readable
       --api-key KEY      the key of the house; or C2C_API_KEY in the
                          environment; absent, the door stands open
       --privacy          no cache, no trace: the sharer's context is
                          dropped, the receiver answers alone (F-17)
       --config FILE      the ini of the served: [serve], [pair], [fuser]
       --fuser-weights PATH
                          the learned weights, from the zoo or from disk

EXIT STATUS
       0  the front served, and stopped, gently
       1  the front could not bind, or the pair is not on the shelf
       2  the usage, wrong

EXAMPLES
       c2c-serve --pair math-small:coder-small -e hf --port 8121 \
                 --certfile certs/cert.pem --keyfile certs/key.pem

       curl https://127.0.0.1:8121/v1/chat/completions \
            -H "authorization: bearer $C2C_API_KEY" \
            -d '{"model": "c2c/math-small+coder-small",
                 "messages": [{"role": "user",
                               "content": "two plus two?"}],
                 "stream": true}'

REPORTING FAULTS
       The failure modes of the front are catalogued in c2c.failures
       as F-9 (the wire, misformed), F-15 (the geometry, mismatched),
       F-17 (the privacy, unhonoured). See c2c(1) and doctor(1).

SEE ALSO
       c2c(1), c2c-proxy(7), c2c-mcp(1), c2c-a2a(7), c2c.config(5)

